      "message": "This file is now identical to the zephyr/program/intelrvp/ptlrvp/src/board_id.c except for the static variable to cache the board id.\n\nThis should be moved into it\u0027s own driver code and shared by fatcat and ocelot.\n\nI think a good location would be\n* zephyr/drivers/board_id/board_id_intel_rvp.c\n\nYou could add a devicetree property for the GPIO controller node that needs to be initialized manually.  \n\n```\n\trvp_board_id: rvp-board-id {\n\t\tcompatible \u003d \"intel,rvp-board-id\";\n\t\tdeferred-init-driver \u003d \u003c\u0026pca95xx\u003e;\n```\n\nYou would register the callback on AP_POWER_STATE_S5 only if the `deferred-init-driver` property is not NULL.\n\n```\n    .deferred_init_driver \u003d DT_INST_PROP_OR(0, deferred_init_driver, NULL),\n    \n    ...\n    \nintel_rvp_board_id_init(const device *device)\n{\n    if (config-\u003edeferred_init_driver) {\n        ap_pwrseq_register_state_entry_callback();\n    }\n}\n```",
